  "scope": "The first clause holds for all nonisomorphic finite simple undirected graph pairs with isomorphic canonical double covers: one has two vertex-disjoint C_k and the other C_(2k), for odd k>=3, including disconnected/bipartite cases. The second clause holds for connected asymmetric unstable graphs in the source scope. More generally, any finite asymmetric graph with an explicit nontrivial TF automorphism has vertex-disjoint C_k and C_(2k). The conditional bundle lemma assumes an odd-order inverse TF pair and a chosen odd moving-orbit quotient cycle, giving C_k plus (M-1)/2 disjoint C_(2k) cycles. Source: [Mizzi arXiv:2603.27559v3 §7](https://arxiv.org/html/2603.27559v3#S7).",
  "status": "independently reviewed written mathematics; novelty unconfirmed; no all-parameter Lean",
  "integration_validation": "exact hashes, Python AST, JSON and dependency closure; no mathematical replay",
